---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { calculateYearsExperience } from '../../lib/experience';

const yearsExperience = calculateYearsExperience();
---

<BaseLayout title="About Me" description="Learn more about Emma Lane - Senior Software Engineer & Tech Lead">
  <div class="about-page">
    <section class="about-hero">
      <img
        src="/images/real-profile-pic.jpg"
    width="200" height="200" decoding="async"
        alt="Emma Lane"
        class="about-hero__image"
      />

      <div class="pressed-hero-flower pressed-hero-flower--bloom" aria-hidden="true">
        <img src="/images/flowers/pressed-bloom.svg" alt="" width="220" height="220" />
      </div>

      <div class="about-hero__copy">
        <p class="home-kicker">About me</p>
        <h1>Hello hello! I'm Emma.</h1>
        <p>
          I'm a Senior Software Engineer and Tech Lead with over {yearsExperience} years of experience across different technologies, projects, and domains.
          I thrive in start-up and scale-up environments, bringing strong technical expertise and leadership to every project.
        </p>
        <p>
          Spark Lane is my digital garden, where I share my journey through code, leadership, creative pursuits and continuous learning.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="about-content-grid">
      <aside class="about-card about-card--side">
        <p class="home-card__eyebrow">Beyond code</p>
        <h2>Curiosity tends to spill over.</h2>
        <p>When I'm not coding, you'll find me exploring creative pursuits, experimenting in the kitchen, working on my latest garden project or diving into gaming worlds. </p>
        <p>Having diverse interests helps me stay curious, approach problems from different angles, and bring fresh perspectives and empathy to technical problem-solving. </p>
        <p>Being neurodivergent shapes how I experience the world, solve problems and communicate. It has given me a strong appreciation for clear information, thoughtful design, flexibility and environments where people can work in ways that suit them.</p>
      </aside>
      
      <section class="about-card about-card--main">
        <!-- Right Column - Tab Navigation and Content -->
        <div class="about-me-container">
          <nav class="about-tabs" aria-label="Tabs">
            <button 
              data-tab="philosophy"
              id="philosophy-btn"
              class="tab-btn active"
            >
              Approach & Philosophy
            </button>
            <button 
              data-tab="space"
              id="space-btn"
              class="tab-btn"
            >
              This Space
            </button>
            <button 
              data-tab="experience"
              id="experience-btn"
              class="tab-btn"
            >
              Experience & Expertise
            </button>
          </nav>
        </div>
        
        <!-- Tab Content -->
        <div class="about-tab-panel">
          <!-- Approach & Philosophy Tab -->
          <div id="philosophy-content" class="tab-content">
            <p>
              I believe in writing clean, maintainable code and creating user experiences that are both functional and delightful. I approach development with an emphasis on accessibility first, continuous learning, community engagement, and user-centred design. By prioritising these principles, I aim to build inclusive experiences that work for everyone, foster a culture of continuous improvement, and contribute to the advancement of the tech industry as a whole.
            </p> 
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Accessibility First</strong>: Building inclusive experiences that work for everyone</li>
              <li><strong>Continuous Learning</strong>: Staying curious and embracing new technologies</li>
              <li><strong>Safe by Design</strong>: Building with privacy, security and people’s trust in mind from the very beginning</li>
              <li><strong>Community Engagement</strong>: Contributing to open source and sharing knowledge</li>
              <li><strong>Tech for Good</strong>: Supporting charities, community groups and projects that make a positive social or environmental difference</li>
              <li><strong>User-Centred Design</strong>: Putting people at the heart of technical decisions</li>              
            </ul>
            <p>
              I regularly assess this site using WAVE and axe to guide accessibility improvements. My <a href="/accessibility-statement/">accessibility statement</a> explains this approach and any known limitations.
            </p>
          </div>
          
          <!-- This Space Tab -->
          <div id="space-content" class="tab-content is-hidden">
            <p>Spark Lane is where I keep the different parts of my work and interests in one place. It is part professional portfolio, part blog, and part digital garden for the things I am learning, making and enjoying. Here you'll find:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Blog Posts</strong>: Technical posts, accessibility thoughts, development notes, research project updates, dissertation updates and the odd personal musing</li>
              <li><strong>Portfolio</strong>: Selected projects that show how I approach software engineering, problem-solving, accessibility and user-centred design</li>
              <li><strong>Research Hub</strong>: My MSc Deepfake Defence project and all related research in one place</li>
              <li><strong>Digital Garden</strong>: Recipes, reading notes, music recommendations, watch lists and cosy gaming references</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          
          <!-- Experience & Expertise Tab -->
          <div id="experience-content" class="tab-content is-hidden">
            <p>With extensive experience across the entire software lifecycle, I've designed, developed and deployed desktop and web-based applications while working with and managing mixed-discipline teams.</p>
            <p>My career has taken me from apprentice and junior developer roles into team leadership, including work as a Team Lead, Tech Lead, Senior Software Engineer and Lead Back-end Developer across fintech, digital agencies and defence.</p>
            <p>I've worked with a diverse modern stack across backend, frontend, CMS, databases, cloud, DevOps and testing.</p>
            <p>To see the bigger picture, take a look at my full CV!</p>

            <p><a href="/about/my-cv/" class="about-contact-card">View my CV</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
    
    <script>
      function showTab(tabName: string) {
        // Hide all content immediately
        document.querySelectorAll('.tab-content').forEach(content => {
          content.classList.add('is-hidden');
          content.classList.remove('tab-fade-in');
        });
        
        // Remove active class from all buttons
        document.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn').forEach(btn => {
          btn.classList.remove('active');
        });
        
        // Show selected content with fade animation
        const selectedContent = document.getElementById(tabName + '-content');
        selectedContent?.classList.remove('is-hidden');
        selectedContent?.classList.add('tab-fade-in');
        
        // Add active class to clicked button
        const activeBtn = document.getElementById(tabName + '-btn');
        activeBtn?.classList.add('active');
        
      }
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.about-tabs [data-tab]').forEach(button => {
        button.addEventListener('click', () => showTab(button.dataset.tab!));
      });
    </script>

    <section class="about-card about-connect-card">
      <p class="home-card__eyebrow">Let's connect</p>
      <h2>Have a project in mind?</h2>
      <p>I'm always excited to connect with my peers. Whether you're interested in collaboration, have a project in mind, or want to discuss leadership and technical challenges, I'd love to hear from you.</p>
      <p><a href="/freelance/">Explore my freelance development services</a>, or get in touch to discuss your project.</p>
      <p>Working on something for a charity or your community? I offer <a href="/freelance/#tech-for-good">tech for good and charity support</a> free of charge or at heavily reduced rates, depending on project scope and availability.</p>

      <div class="button-group">
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/emmalouiselane/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="about-contact-card">
          <span class="about-card__cta">LinkedIn</span>
        </a>
        <a href="mailto:emma@sparklane.dev" class="about-contact-card">
          <span class="about-card__cta">Email me</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="about-connect-card__discord">Prefer a more informal chat? Add me on Discord as <strong>sparklane</strong>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
